{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "U1: Reimplement locally, on top of the already-externalized protos (protos/common, protos/msp, protos/peer), the small policy-construction logic that statebased currently pulls in via common/cauthdsl, and replace pkg/errors with the Go standard library so that the only remaining fabric imports are the protos.",
    "U2: Replace BCCSP-based symmetric encryption in the entities package with Go standard library cryptography (crypto/aes, crypto/cipher, crypto/rand) and drop flogging in favor of minimal/no logging, keeping the public API stable for existing chaincode authors.",
    "U5: Externalize protoutil into a new standalone Go module 'fabric-lib-go'; move the tiny internal/pkg/identity interfaces (e.g., SigningIdentity) into the module and copy the few small helpers from common/util that protoutil needs, so the module depends only on fabric-protos-go and external libraries.",
    "U6: Externalize BCCSP (core interfaces, factory, signer, utils, sw, pkcs11 and idemix providers) into a dedicated Go module, replacing the flogging dependency with a small pluggable Logger interface with a no-op default.",
    "U7: Externalize MSP into a dedicated Go module that depends on the externalized BCCSP module and fabric-protos-go, replacing flogging with the same pluggable logger approach.",
    "U8: Externalize the discovery client into a dedicated Go module, decoupling it from fabric/gossip and fabric/comm by introducing narrow local interfaces for peer membership and GRPC connection management.",
    "Each externalized component ships as an independent Go module with its own go.mod, semantic versioning, README, license and CI (GitHub Actions: build, unit tests with -race, golangci-lint, go mod tidy verification).",
    "Existing unit tests are migrated together with the code, and a small smoke-test consumer module per library proves the module can be 'go get'-ed and used without the fabric core repository.",
    "U3 and U4 are duplicate requests for the same marbles02_private comment change in fabric-samples and are delivered as a single change.",
    "The fabric core repository is not rewritten to consume the new externalized modules within this increment; the deliverables are the standalone consumable modules plus validation."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "One experienced Go developer with good knowledge of the Fabric codebase performs all work full-time; estimates are effort (workdays), not elapsed calendar time.",
    "Target repositories (fabric-lib-go, fabric-bccsp, fabric-msp, fabric-discovery-client or similar names) are provisioned by Hyperledger maintainers; org governance, approvals and account/permission setup are outside the development effort.",
    "fabric-protos-go already exists and is the canonical source of the protobuf-generated code; no proto definition changes are needed.",
    "Go modules are used throughout (Go 1.12+ era toolchain, fabric ~2.x code state).",
    "Typical code-review feedback/rework cycles are included within the activity estimates; formal QA, security audits and performance testing are out of scope.",
    "No functional behavior changes are intended; API compatibility is preserved so the Fabric Go SDK can drop its internal copies and consume the externalized modules.",
    "The idemix-based BCCSP providers are included in the BCCSP externalization scope.",
    "For U3/U4 only comment/example changes in the fabric-samples marbles02_private chaincode are required, plus manual verification of the corrected export command on a bash shell; no Windows-specific code changes are needed."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "1.1",
      "activity_name": "Analyze shim ext dependency graphs and agree refactoring design",
      "activity_description": "Run go list dependency analysis for statebased and entities, identify exactly which imports pull in cauthdsl, protoutil, bccsp and flogging, and document the refactoring design for U1 and U2.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "1.2",
      "activity_name": "Refactor statebased package to protos-only fabric imports (U1)",
      "activity_description": "Remove cauthdsl/protoutil/pkg-errors usage from core/chaincode/shim/ext/statebased by constructing signature policy envelopes directly with protos types and standard library error handling.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "1.3",
      "activity_name": "Test and verify statebased acceptance criteria (U1)",
      "activity_description": "Update/run unit tests and verify via 'go list' that the only fabric imports of the statebased package are the protos packages.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "1.4",
      "activity_name": "Refactor entities package to remove fabric dependencies (U2)",
      "activity_description": "Replace BCCSP-based encryption in core/chaincode/shim/ext/entities with standard library AES crypto and remove flogging usage while keeping the public API unchanged.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "1.5",
      "activity_name": "Test and verify entities acceptance criteria (U2)",
      "activity_description": "Update/run unit tests and verify via 'go list' that the entities package no longer drags in bccsp, flogging or other fabric packages.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "2.1",
      "activity_name": "Fix marbles02_private export command comments in fabric-samples (U3, U4)",
      "activity_description": "Add the 'tr -d \\n' guidance to the base64 export examples in the marbles02_private sample chaincode comments, manually verify the corrected commands in a bash shell, and submit the change to fabric-samples.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "3.1",
      "activity_name": "Analyze protoutil dependencies and design module boundary (U5)",
      "activity_description": "Map protoutil's internal dependencies (internal/pkg/identity, common/util, etc.) and design the fabric-lib-go module layout and decoupling approach.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "3.2",
      "activity_name": "Scaffold fabric-lib-go repository and CI",
      "activity_description": "Create go.mod, license, README, lint configuration and GitHub Actions CI pipeline (build, unit tests with -race, go mod tidy check) for the new protoutil module.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "3.3",
      "activity_name": "Migrate protoutil code and tests into fabric-lib-go (U5)",
      "activity_description": "Move protoutil source and unit tests into the new module, move/copy the small identity interfaces and utility helpers it needs, and remove all fabric-core imports.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "3.4",
      "activity_name": "Validate, version and smoke-test fabric-lib-go",
      "activity_description": "Get CI green, tag an initial semantic version, and validate consumption from a small standalone consumer module mimicking the SDK usage.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "4.1",
      "activity_name": "Analyze BCCSP dependency graph and design externalization (U6)",
      "activity_description": "Map dependencies of bccsp core, factory, signer, utils, sw, pkcs11 and idemix providers on fabric packages (flogging, idemix, protos) and design the decoupling approach.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "4.2",
      "activity_name": "Scaffold BCCSP repository and CI",
      "activity_description": "Create the BCCSP Go module with go.mod, license, README, lint config and CI pipeline including pkcs11 build-tag aware test jobs.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "4.3",
      "activity_name": "Migrate BCCSP core code and tests (U6)",
      "activity_description": "Move BCCSP interfaces, factory, signer, sw and utils packages plus tests into the new module and replace flogging with the pluggable logger interface.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "4.4",
      "activity_name": "Migrate BCCSP pkcs11 and idemix providers and tests (U6)",
      "activity_description": "Move the pkcs11 and idemix BCCSP providers (bridge, handlers) and their tests into the module, resolving dependencies on fabric/idemix and protos.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "4.5",
      "activity_name": "Validate, version and smoke-test BCCSP module",
      "activity_description": "Get CI green, tag an initial version and validate consumption of the externalized BCCSP from a standalone consumer module.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "5.1",
      "activity_name": "Analyze MSP dependencies and design externalization (U7)",
      "activity_description": "Map MSP dependencies on bccsp, protos, flogging and related packages and design the module based on the already-externalized BCCSP.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "5.2",
      "activity_name": "Scaffold MSP repository and CI",
      "activity_description": "Create the MSP Go module with go.mod, license, README, lint config and CI pipeline.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "5.3",
      "activity_name": "Migrate MSP code and tests (U7)",
      "activity_description": "Move the msp package and its tests into the new module, switch its bccsp imports to the externalized BCCSP module and replace flogging with the pluggable logger.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "5.4",
      "activity_name": "Validate, version and smoke-test MSP module",
      "activity_description": "Get CI green, tag an initial version and validate consumption of the externalized MSP from a standalone consumer module.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "6.1",
      "activity_name": "Analyze discovery client dependencies and design externalization (U8)",
      "activity_description": "Map discovery/client dependencies on fabric gossip, comm and protos packages and design narrow local interfaces for membership and GRPC connection management.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "6.2",
      "activity_name": "Scaffold discovery client repository and CI",
      "activity_description": "Create the discovery client Go module with go.mod, license, README, lint config and CI pipeline.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "6.3",
      "activity_name": "Migrate discovery client code and tests (U8)",
      "activity_description": "Move the discovery client and its tests into the new module, decoupling it from fabric/gossip and fabric/comm via the designed interfaces.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "6.4",
      "activity_name": "Validate, version and smoke-test discovery client module",
      "activity_description": "Get CI green, tag an initial version and validate consumption of the externalized discovery client from a standalone consumer module.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "7.1",
      "activity_name": "Cross-repo documentation and final integration validation",
      "activity_description": "Write migration/usage documentation for SDK maintainers covering the externalized modules and perform a final end-to-end validation of all deliverables.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 47
  }
}

